.page touch 1 create empty files

# SYNOPSIS
*touch* _FILE_...

# DESCRIPTION
`touch` creates each _FILE_ as an empty file (mode 644) if it does not exist. A file that already exists is opened and left exactly as it is: in this system `touch` does not change modification times. Words that start with a dash are ignored.

# EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 if a file could not be created.

# EXAMPLES
    touch notes.txt
    touch a b c

# SEE ALSO
mkdir(1), mktemp(1), stat(1)
